{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "evaluation schemes for x^2 under gt1030\npolynomial of degree 2 in x:\n  as written cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x^2\n  pow()      cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x^2\n  products   cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  Horner     cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  Estrin     cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  (depth is the critical path: Estrin trades operations for parallelism)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "scheme", "ucas": "scheme x^2", "structured": false, "result": {"text": "evaluation schemes for x^2 under gt1030\npolynomial of degree 2 in x:\n  as written cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x^2\n  pow()      cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x^2\n  products   cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  Horner     cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  Estrin     cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  (depth is the critical path: Estrin trades operations for parallelism)\n"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "evaluation schemes for x^2 under gt1030\npolynomial of degree 2 in x:\n  as written cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x^2\n  pow()      cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x^2\n  products   cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  Horner     cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  Estrin     cost 1      depth 1      1 ops  x*x\n             bit-identical at 201 points\n  (depth is the critical path: Estrin trades operations for parallelism)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "evaluation schemes for x^3 - 3x under gt1030\npolynomial of degree 3 in x:\n  as written cost 10     depth 9      3 ops  x^3 - 3x\n  pow()      cost 10     depth 9      3 ops  x^3 - 3x\n  products   cost 4      depth 3      4 ops  x*x*x - 3x\n             max relative difference 4.4e-16 (rounding) at 201 points\n  Horner     cost 3      depth 3      3 ops  (x*x - 3)*x\n             max relative difference 2.2e-15 (rounding) at 201 points\n  Estrin     cost 4      depth 3      4 ops  x*(x*x) - 3x\n             max relative difference 4.4e-16 (rounding) at 201 points\n  (depth is the critical path: Estrin trades operations for parallelism)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "scheme", "ucas": "scheme x^3 - 3x", "structured": false, "result": {"text": "evaluation schemes for x^3 - 3x under gt1030\npolynomial of degree 3 in x:\n  as written cost 10     depth 9      3 ops  x^3 - 3x\n  pow()      cost 10     depth 9      3 ops  x^3 - 3x\n  products   cost 4      depth 3      4 ops  x*x*x - 3x\n             max relative difference 4.4e-16 (rounding) at 201 points\n  Horner     cost 3      depth 3      3 ops  (x*x - 3)*x\n             max relative difference 2.2e-15 (rounding) at 201 points\n  Estrin     cost 4      depth 3      4 ops  x*(x*x) - 3x\n             max relative difference 4.4e-16 (rounding) at 201 points\n  (depth is the critical path: Estrin trades operations for parallelism)\n"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "evaluation schemes for x^3 - 3x under gt1030\npolynomial of degree 3 in x:\n  as written cost 10     depth 9      3 ops  x^3 - 3x\n  pow()      cost 10     depth 9      3 ops  x^3 - 3x\n  products   cost 4      depth 3      4 ops  x*x*x - 3x\n             max relative difference 4.4e-16 (rounding) at 201 points\n  Horner     cost 3      depth 3      3 ops  (x*x - 3)*x\n             max relative difference 2.2e-15 (roundin